# Testing Rules

## Framework

Use `pytest`.

Tests must be deterministic and independently executable.

## Test Structure

Prefer Arrange / Act / Assert:

```python
# Arrange
...

# Act
...

# Assert
...
```

## Naming

Test names must describe behavior.

Good:

```python
def test_should_reject_product_when_price_is_zero():
    ...
```

Avoid:

```python
def test_product_1():
    ...
```

## Unit Tests

Unit tests should cover:

- domain rules;
- application use cases;
- validation;
- error conditions;
- idempotency behavior;
- calculations.

Keep unit tests isolated from external infrastructure.

## Integration Tests

Integration tests should cover relevant boundaries:

- PostgreSQL;
- Redis;
- RabbitMQ;
- HTTP service integration.

Prefer real infrastructure in integration tests when practical instead of mocking the entire system.

## Mocks

Do not mock everything.

Mock external boundaries when isolation is the purpose of the test.

Do not mock the class under test.

## Regression

When fixing a reproducible bug, add a regression test when practical.

## Test Quality

Tests should verify behavior, not implementation details.

Avoid tests that break merely because internal class structure changes while behavior remains correct.
